                                                "sense_id": "8578afca-f42c-33f7-bdc0-86c5b125e5e8",
                                                "text": "Ants are integral components of terrestrial ecosystems, owing to their manifold interactions with other organisms. They serve as seed dispersers for plants (myrmecochory), mutualists with sap-sucking insects (trophobionts), and hosts for a wide range of associate organisms (myrmecophiles) and act as both predator and prey."
